WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.669 --> 00:00:05.050
Donald Trump received some of his best polling
in a while yesterday.

00:00:05.050 --> 00:00:11.830
There's a major new poll from CNN which has
Joe Biden only four points ahead of Donald

00:00:11.830 --> 00:00:14.110
Trump with the margin of error.

00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:16.630
That could mean Trump is now straight up winning.

00:00:16.630 --> 00:00:19.380
This is one of the closest polls in a while.

00:00:19.380 --> 00:00:25.779
It's not the only one that says the race is
this close, but it should be a huge warning

00:00:25.779 --> 00:00:31.490
to anybody who thinks Joe Biden has this in
the bag, especially if you thought yesterday's

00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:34.479
first day of the DNC was not so good.

00:00:34.479 --> 00:00:42.010
Then we have nothing to sit back and be complacent
about if we look at recent national polls.

00:00:42.010 --> 00:00:48.089
CNN now has Biden only plus four, and otherwise
it's a bunch of Biden plus seven, Biden plus

00:00:48.089 --> 00:00:50.489
nine, Biden plus 10.

00:00:50.489 --> 00:00:56.109
Other than a Harris sex poll from a week ago,
which agrees it's Biden up by four.

00:00:56.109 --> 00:01:02.489
Now, if we look at this CNN poll more closely,
you will see that the margin of error is three

00:01:02.489 --> 00:01:03.729
point seven.

00:01:03.729 --> 00:01:10.549
OK, so that means that the poll says that
this is not speculation.

00:01:10.549 --> 00:01:11.549
Instead of 50.

00:01:11.549 --> 00:01:16.170
Biden might only have forty six point three
instead of 46.

00:01:16.170 --> 00:01:18.229
Trump could have forty nine point seven.

00:01:18.229 --> 00:01:23.450
So this poll, if you read it correctly and
understand the margin of error, the poll says

00:01:23.450 --> 00:01:26.920
that right now Trump could be up by three
point four.

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:32.829
Now, I don't need to remind you that in 2016,
Hillary Clinton had a lead of three in the

00:01:32.829 --> 00:01:36.280
national polls and she ended up winning by
two.

00:01:36.280 --> 00:01:40.710
From the standpoint of the popular vote and
lost the Electoral College, as Michelle Obama

00:01:40.710 --> 00:01:45.880
astutely pointed out yesterday, this is a
poll which says, forget about whether Biden

00:01:45.880 --> 00:01:48.280
is up three or four.

00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:51.890
Trump could be up three nationally right now.

00:01:51.890 --> 00:01:58.320
This poll outlines a better situation for
Donald Trump today than he had in November

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:00.210
of 2016.

00:02:00.210 --> 00:02:02.729
Now it's one poll.

00:02:02.729 --> 00:02:07.860
The average lead for Biden remains just under
eight points.

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:09.670
But why would we take any chance?

00:02:09.670 --> 00:02:13.959
The polling is looking more and more like
it did in 2016.

00:02:13.959 --> 00:02:16.700
Anyone thinking this is over needs to check
the facts.

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:21.500
And the facts are that not only is the polling
tightening between Biden and Trump, Trump's

00:02:21.500 --> 00:02:22.880
approval is climbing.

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:29.040
I know that when we think about facts and
reason, it is crazy to think that this would

00:02:29.040 --> 00:02:30.239
be going on.

00:02:30.239 --> 00:02:34.819
But we live in a country where more than 60
million people voted for the guy in 2016.

00:02:34.819 --> 00:02:37.470
So we have to expect things that make no sense.

00:02:37.470 --> 00:02:42.260
And if you look at the Gallup Trump approval
tracking poll, you see that after a huge drop

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:47.069
in approval during the earlier phases of the
Corona virus pandemic, Donald Trump's approval

00:02:47.069 --> 00:02:55.830
has slowly but surely started to creep back
up from a low of 38 back in whenever up to

00:02:55.830 --> 00:02:57.569
39, 40, 42.

00:02:57.569 --> 00:03:00.730
And the trend is pointing further up.

00:03:00.730 --> 00:03:03.500
Now we can debate why this is happening.

00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:05.459
Some people are falling for Trump's B.S.

00:03:05.459 --> 00:03:07.410
They're just falling for it.

00:03:07.410 --> 00:03:10.750
We have a crazy situation that has been normalized
to some degree.

00:03:10.750 --> 00:03:15.450
And people have gotten used to the pandemic
and used to thousands of people dying every

00:03:15.450 --> 00:03:17.329
single week from Corona virus.

00:03:17.329 --> 00:03:18.689
There are some people that are just dumb.

00:03:18.689 --> 00:03:19.689
Okay.

00:03:19.689 --> 00:03:20.689
Oh, find that's some beat.

00:03:20.689 --> 00:03:21.860
It doesn't matter.

00:03:21.860 --> 00:03:22.860
That's the thing.

00:03:22.860 --> 00:03:25.019
They get to vote and we get to vote.

00:03:25.019 --> 00:03:31.040
Our focus needs to be getting out the vote
and making sure that we vote.

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:32.819
This is not it.

00:03:32.819 --> 00:03:37.620
If you looked at Biden plus fifteen and an
outlier polls six weeks ago and thought this

00:03:37.620 --> 00:03:39.380
was going to be easy.

00:03:39.380 --> 00:03:42.129
This is not going to be easy.

00:03:42.129 --> 00:03:43.660
This is not going to be easy.

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:45.390
Two and a half months to go.

00:03:45.390 --> 00:03:49.360
We could see anything happen between now and
November.

00:03:49.360 --> 00:03:50.360
Trump teasing.

00:03:50.360 --> 00:03:52.370
He's going to pardon someone major today.

00:03:52.370 --> 00:03:53.980
Who knows what that is.

00:03:53.980 --> 00:03:54.980
He mentioned it.

00:03:54.980 --> 00:03:58.080
He said it's not Snowden today, but he's now
thinking about.

00:03:58.080 --> 00:04:01.700
We don't know how different elements of the
electorate could react.

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:02.910
We have no control over it.

00:04:02.910 --> 00:04:07.739
We only have control over our voting and talking
to other people about the importance of voting.

